### CoSERV Progress Update
* Presentation: [CoSERV Progress Update](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rats-coserv-progress-update-00)
* Speaker: **Paul Howard**
* Specification: [`draft-ietf-rats-coserv`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-rats-coserv/)
* **Key Updates**:
  * Finalized topological queries and query results for composited attester trust dependencies in v08.
  * Addressed feedback from the HTTP Directorate review.
  * Tracked normative integration with Concise TA Stores via [`draft-ietf-rats-concise-ta-stores`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-rats-concise-ta-stores/).
  * Highlighted running code within the Veraison project (Golang server, Rust client) and new multi-role deployment support created by Fujitsu and Arm to allow decoupled endorsement services and verification services.
* **Discussion**:
  * **Sam** inquired about the exact role of CoSERV in decoupled deployments; **Paul Howard** confirmed CoSERV serves as the query language used by verification services to retrieve endorsement data from endorsement services.
  * **Shalini Bajaj** asked if multiple endorsement services are supported; **Paul Howard** confirmed CoSERV queries operate independently of server cardinality.

