### EAR and AR4SI Update
* Presentation: [EAR and AR4SI update](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rats-ear-and-ar4si-update-01)
* Speaker: **Thomas Fossati**
* Specifications: [`draft-ietf-rats-ear`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-rats-ear/) and [`draft-ietf-rats-ar4si`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-rats-ar4si/)
* **Key Updates**:
  * Added the `incomplete` status tier to separate internal sub-verifier errors or unparseable client inputs from the `none` trust tier.
  * Extended EAR for multi-verifier environments by introducing device topology claims (adjacency lists) and allowing nested EAR sub-mods.
  * Added free-form diagnostic text claims, input digest claims for binding request contexts, and typed CBOR evidence records.
* **Discussion & Next Steps**:
  * Discussed splitting hardware and firmware trust buckets and refining identity claim modeling.
  * Plan to freeze feature development following implementation feedback from Confidential Containers, Azure, NVIDIA, and Veraison prior to working group reviews.

