### Epoch Markers Update
* Presentation: [Epoch Markers update](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rats-epoch-markers-update-02)
* Speaker: **Hank Birkholz**
* Specification: [`draft-ietf-rats-epoch-markers`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-rats-epoch-markers/)
* **Key Updates**:
  * Introduced the `epoclet` (a nonce-sized digest of an epoch marker/freshness construct suitable for CMW transport in constrained headers).
  * Added MIME types, CoAP Content-Formats, and support for CBOR time tags (tags 1 and 1001) alongside specialized epoch tick tags.
  * Added CBOR-based epoch marker claims for JWT/CWT and COSE headers, created an Extended Key Usage (EKU) for X.509 epoch bail endorsements, and aligned handle usage with [`draft-ietf-rats-reference-interaction-models`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-rats-reference-interaction-models/).
* **Discussion**:
  * **Thomas Fossati** asked about IANA allocation strategy; **Hank Birkholz** noted early allocations would be requested for SMI/EKU and CBOR tags.
  * **Shalini Bajaj** asked if Epoch IDs accompany or replace nonces; **Hank Birkholz** clarified that Epoch Markers act as substitutes for nonces in streaming/broadcast freshness models (or use `epoclets` when space-constrained).

